# Source: Gilly1970/Gemtek-W1700K-6.18 openwrt-patches/ 047+034+035+036+042+026+044（2026-09-10；B-1 调研实测 APPLIES）
# Upstream: 部分已上游/部分自持：034（reg_lock irqsave）与 047（restart NPU）无上游提交；035/036/042/026/044 为竞态与越界加固。
# Reason: ① 047——上游 mt7996_mac_restart() 只重启 WED；NPU 板整机复位后 NPU 仍持有旧环/描述符地址，
#   host TX 永死；且两个 NAPI 循环只对 WED 跳过 RRO 队列，NPU 下会对未 napi_add 的 RRO/TXFREE 队列
#   napi_disable() → 解引用 NULL oops。修：补 NPU/RRO/TXFREE 跳过 + 复位后重新 __mt7996_npu_hw_init()。
#   ② 034——mt7996 mmio reg_lock 用 spin_lock_bh，在中断上下文竞争时可致 AP panic → 改 irqsave。
#   ③ 035——mt76_tx_status_skb_add() 的 wcid 检查在锁外且只判指针非空 → 加 wcid 相等校验 + NO_ACK 兜底。
#   ④ 036——mt76_reset_device() 的 wcid 拆除顺序（先清 dev->wcid 再 cleanup）→ 修正顺序。
#   ⑤ 042——断连包（disassoc）队列分配走错队列 → 与 deauth 一并判入管理帧路径。
#   ⑥ 026——ALL_STA_INFO 事件未校验 sta_num/tag → 按 tag 计算 elem_size 并做长度校验。
#   ⑦ 044——ie_countdown TLV 解析未校验 len → 加上界与最小长度校验。
# 验证：对 openwrt/mt76 be5ce7910521492d4a2e4ce7ee3843680a46c047 真实源码逐条 patch -p1 命中
#   （026/044 偏移 237 行系 Gilly 基线前进，命中成功；034 偏移 26 行；047 与 mt76-0010/0013 同文件
#   顺序共存实证通过）。内层对本仓 mt76 包为新增文件，构建时由 patch-kernel.sh glob 应用。
# 未验证：无运行时验证；047 的判据 = 整机复位后 host TX 恢复（dmesg 无 NAPI NULL oops）。
# !!! 2026-09-15 P19/B 隔离实验（F172 实机失败后）：删除内层 047 的 full-reset 停 NPU hunk
#   （13 行；外层 @@ -0,0 +1,85 @@ -> +1,72）。只保留 NAPI 跳过与复位后 __mt7996_npu_hw_init() 重入。
#   目的 = 隔离「NPU stop 是否触发 CmpltTO / 固件 patch semaphore 卡死」；**不是修法**，无效即回退。
#EXP diff --git a/package/kernel/mt76/patches/047-wifi-mt76-mt7996-restart-npu-on-full-chip-reset.patch b/package/kernel/mt76/patches/047-wifi-mt76-mt7996-restart-npu-on-full-chip-reset.patch
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/package/kernel/mt76/patches/047-wifi-mt76-mt7996-restart-npu-on-full-chip-reset.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,72 @@
+From: Gilly <gilroyscott1970@gmail.com>
+Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
+Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: re-init the NPU after a full chip reset
+
+The L1 SER path stops the NPU, re-hands it the new rings once DMA is back, 
+and keeps NAPI off the NPU-owned RRO and TX-free queues. A full chip reset 
+(WM/WA watchdog) takes the mt7996_mac_full_reset() path instead, which 
+restarts WED but has no NPU equivalent. So on an NPU board the NPU is never 
+stopped and never learns the ring addresses recreated by the WFSYS reset, 
+and since host TX also runs through the NPU rings, Wi-Fi stays dead until 
+reboot. Worse, the NAPI loops only skip RRO queues when WED is active, so 
+under NPU napi_disable() runs on queues that were allocated but never had 
+NAPI added, and the dereference of their NULL device pointer oopses. 
+
+Re-apply the L1 path's queue skips to both NAPI loops, and re-initialise the 
+NPU right after 
+the WED restart, failing the restart on error so it is retried rather than 
+left with host TX dead. Found by auditing the WED-only paths for missing 
+NPU handling; not yet exercised on-device, as full chip resets are rare.
+
+Signed-off-by: Gilly <gilroyscott1970@gmail.com>
+---
+diff --git a/mt7996/mac.c b/mt7996/mac.c
+index 976a0932..4e78c9af 100644
+--- a/mt7996/mac.c
++++ b/mt7996/mac.c
+@@ -2325,6 +2325,13 @@ mt7996_mac_restart(struct mt7996_dev *dev)
+ 		    mt76_queue_is_wed_rro(&mdev->q_rx[i]))
+ 			continue;
+ 
++		if (mt76_npu_device_active(mdev) &&
++		    mt76_queue_is_wed_rro(&mdev->q_rx[i]))
++			continue;
++
++		if (mt76_queue_is_npu_txfree(&mdev->q_rx[i]))
++			continue;
++
+ 		if (mdev->q_rx[i].ndesc)
+ 			napi_disable(&dev->mt76.napi[i]);
+ 	}
+@@ -2341,6 +2348,13 @@ mt7996_mac_restart(struct mt7996_dev *dev)
+ 		    mt76_queue_is_wed_rro(&mdev->q_rx[i]))
+ 			continue;
+ 
++		if (mt76_npu_device_active(mdev) &&
++		    mt76_queue_is_wed_rro(&mdev->q_rx[i]))
++			continue;
++
++		if (mt76_queue_is_npu_txfree(&mdev->q_rx[i]))
++			continue;
++
+ 		if (mdev->q_rx[i].ndesc) {
+ 			napi_enable(&dev->mt76.napi[i]);
+ 			local_bh_disable();
+@@ -2394,6 +2408,17 @@ mt7996_mac_restart(struct mt7996_dev *dev)
+ 				     MT_INT_TX_RX_DONE_EXT);
+ 	}
+ 
++	/* The NPU still holds the ring and descriptor addresses from before
++	 * the reset. Hand it the new ones, as the L1 recovery path does. Host
++	 * TX runs through the NPU rings too, so treat a failure like any other
++	 * init step and let mt7996_mac_full_reset() retry the restart.
++	 */
++	ret = __mt7996_npu_hw_init(dev);
++	if (ret) {
++		dev_err(mdev->dev, "NPU re-init after full reset failed: %d\n", ret);
++		goto out;
++	}
++
+ 	/* set the necessary init items */
+ 	ret = mt7996_mcu_set_eeprom(dev);
+ 	if (ret)
diff --git a/package/kernel/mt76/patches/034-wifi-mt76-mt7996-reg_lock-irqsave-prevent-AP-panic.patch b/package/kernel/mt76/patches/034-wifi-mt76-mt7996-reg_lock-irqsave-prevent-AP-panic.patch
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/package/kernel/mt76/patches/034-wifi-mt76-mt7996-reg_lock-irqsave-prevent-AP-panic.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,89 @@
+From 3edfc0cbf7dc666a0b051b54f51634d6ff2a3be6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Shayne Chen <shayne.chen@mediatek.com>
+Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: use irqsave on reg_lock to prevent AP panic
+
+AP panic (Asynchronous SError) can occur when the MT7996 register remap
+window (protected by dev->reg_lock) is accessed from hardirq context:
+spin_lock_bh does not disable hardirqs, so an interrupt can reenter the
+remap window mid-access. Use spin_lock_irqsave/irqrestore instead.
+
+Rebased onto OpenWrt mt76 pin be5ce791 (2026-09-01): upstream 69f26dbae7 changed the
+addr test to INVALID_REG_ADDR. Previously rebased onto b2704cf5 (2026-08-01); original MTK context
+was cut against an older base. Original: gerrit 12465539 (mtk-openwrt-feeds).
+
+Signed-off-by: Shayne Chen <shayne.chen@mediatek.com>
+---
+--- a/mt7996/mmio.c
++++ b/mt7996/mmio.c
+@@ -365,29 +365,31 @@
+ 			  size_t len)
+ {
+ 	u32 addr = __mt7996_reg_addr(dev, offset);
++	unsigned long flags;
+ 
+ 	if (addr != INVALID_REG_ADDR) {
+ 		memcpy_fromio(buf, dev->mt76.mmio.regs + addr, len);
+ 		return;
+ 	}
+ 
+-	spin_lock_bh(&dev->reg_lock);
++	spin_lock_irqsave(&dev->reg_lock, flags);
+ 	memcpy_fromio(buf, dev->mt76.mmio.regs +
+ 			   __mt7996_reg_remap_addr(dev, offset), len);
+-	spin_unlock_bh(&dev->reg_lock);
++	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&dev->reg_lock, flags);
+ }
+ 
+ static u32 mt7996_rr(struct mt76_dev *mdev, u32 offset)
+ {
+ 	struct mt7996_dev *dev = container_of(mdev, struct mt7996_dev, mt76);
+ 	u32 addr = __mt7996_reg_addr(dev, offset), val;
++	unsigned long flags;
+ 
+ 	if (addr != INVALID_REG_ADDR)
+ 		return dev->bus_ops->rr(mdev, addr);
+ 
+-	spin_lock_bh(&dev->reg_lock);
++	spin_lock_irqsave(&dev->reg_lock, flags);
+ 	val = dev->bus_ops->rr(mdev, __mt7996_reg_remap_addr(dev, offset));
+-	spin_unlock_bh(&dev->reg_lock);
++	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&dev->reg_lock, flags);
+ 
+ 	return val;
+ }
+@@ -396,28 +398,30 @@
+ {
+ 	struct mt7996_dev *dev = container_of(mdev, struct mt7996_dev, mt76);
+ 	u32 addr = __mt7996_reg_addr(dev, offset);
++	unsigned long flags;
+ 
+ 	if (addr != INVALID_REG_ADDR) {
+ 		dev->bus_ops->wr(mdev, addr, val);
+ 		return;
+ 	}
+ 
+-	spin_lock_bh(&dev->reg_lock);
++	spin_lock_irqsave(&dev->reg_lock, flags);
+ 	dev->bus_ops->wr(mdev, __mt7996_reg_remap_addr(dev, offset), val);
+-	spin_unlock_bh(&dev->reg_lock);
++	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&dev->reg_lock, flags);
+ }
+ 
+ static u32 mt7996_rmw(struct mt76_dev *mdev, u32 offset, u32 mask, u32 val)
+ {
+ 	struct mt7996_dev *dev = container_of(mdev, struct mt7996_dev, mt76);
+ 	u32 addr = __mt7996_reg_addr(dev, offset);
++	unsigned long flags;
+ 
+ 	if (addr != INVALID_REG_ADDR)
+ 		return dev->bus_ops->rmw(mdev, addr, mask, val);
+ 
+-	spin_lock_bh(&dev->reg_lock);
++	spin_lock_irqsave(&dev->reg_lock, flags);
+ 	val = dev->bus_ops->rmw(mdev, __mt7996_reg_remap_addr(dev, offset), mask, val);
+-	spin_unlock_bh(&dev->reg_lock);
++	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&dev->reg_lock, flags);
+ 
+ 	return val;
+ }
+
diff --git a/package/kernel/mt76/patches/035-wifi-mt76-fix-unlocked-wcid-check-in-mt76_tx_status_skb_add.patch b/package/kernel/mt76/patches/035-wifi-mt76-fix-unlocked-wcid-check-in-mt76_tx_status_skb_add.patch
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/package/kernel/mt76/patches/035-wifi-mt76-fix-unlocked-wcid-check-in-mt76_tx_status_skb_add.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,46 @@
+From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Ryan Leung <lrd.airoha@gmail.com>
+Date: Fri, 22 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
+Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: fix unlocked wcid check in mt76_tx_status_skb_add
+
+mt76_tx_status_skb_add() tested whether the wcid was still published
+(rcu_access_pointer(dev->wcid[wcid->idx])) OUTSIDE dev->status_lock.
+Between that test passing and taking the lock to allocate a packet id
+into wcid->pktid, the wcid can be torn down and unpublished, or its
+index reused for a different station.  The stale/reused wcid then gets a
+pktid allocated and is linked onto dev->wcid_list, so TX status is later
+accounted against a wcid that is no longer the owner of that index.
+
+Drop the unlocked test (keep only the !wcid guard) and instead verify,
+under status_lock, that dev->wcid[wcid->idx] still points at THIS wcid
+before allocating.  The pointer-identity check also rejects index reuse,
+which the previous non-NULL test did not catch.  The WED / NO_ACK fast
+paths return before the lock is taken, so the offload hot path is
+unaffected.
+
+Signed-off-by: Ryan Leung <lrd.airoha@gmail.com>
+---
+--- a/tx.c
++++ b/tx.c
+@@ -129,7 +129,7 @@ mt76_tx_status_skb_add(struct mt76_dev *dev, struct mt76_wcid *wcid,
+
+ 	memset(cb, 0, sizeof(*cb));
+
+-	if (!wcid || !rcu_access_pointer(dev->wcid[wcid->idx]))
++	if (!wcid)
+ 		return MT_PACKET_ID_NO_ACK;
+
+ 	if (info->flags & IEEE80211_TX_CTL_NO_ACK)
+@@ -147,6 +147,11 @@ mt76_tx_status_skb_add(struct mt76_dev *dev, struct mt76_wcid *wcid,
+
+ 	spin_lock_bh(&dev->status_lock);
+
++	if (rcu_access_pointer(dev->wcid[wcid->idx]) != wcid) {
++		pid = MT_PACKET_ID_NO_ACK;
++		goto out;
++	}
++
+ 	pid = idr_alloc(&wcid->pktid, skb, MT_PACKET_ID_FIRST,
+ 			MT_PACKET_ID_MASK, GFP_ATOMIC);
+ 	if (pid < 0) {
+
diff --git a/package/kernel/mt76/patches/036-wifi-mt76-fix-wcid-teardown-ordering-in-mt76_reset_device.patch b/package/kernel/mt76/patches/036-wifi-mt76-fix-wcid-teardown-ordering-in-mt76_reset_device.patch
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/package/kernel/mt76/patches/036-wifi-mt76-fix-wcid-teardown-ordering-in-mt76_reset_device.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,28 @@
+From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Ryan Leung <lrd.airoha@gmail.com>
+Date: Fri, 22 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
+Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: fix wcid teardown ordering in mt76_reset_device
+
+mt76_reset_device() ran mt76_wcid_cleanup() while the wcid was still
+published in dev->wcid[i], only clearing the pointer afterwards.  During
+cleanup the wcid is therefore still reachable by concurrent lookups (TX
+status, RX), which can grab and use a wcid that is being torn down.
+
+Unpublish first: NULL dev->wcid[i], then run mt76_wcid_cleanup().  This
+mirrors the correct add ordering (publish last) so no new lookup can find
+the wcid once teardown has begun.
+
+Signed-off-by: Ryan Leung <lrd.airoha@gmail.com>
+---
+--- a/mac80211.c
++++ b/mac80211.c
+@@ -856,8 +856,8 @@ void mt76_reset_device(struct mt76_dev *dev)
+ 			continue;
+
+ 		wcid->sta = 0;
+-		mt76_wcid_cleanup(dev, wcid);
+ 		rcu_assign_pointer(dev->wcid[i], NULL);
++		mt76_wcid_cleanup(dev, wcid);
+ 	}
+ 	rcu_read_unlock();
+
diff --git a/package/kernel/mt76/patches/042-wifi-mt76-fix-queue-assignment-for-disassoc-packets.patch b/package/kernel/mt76/patches/042-wifi-mt76-fix-queue-assignment-for-disassoc-packets.patch
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/package/kernel/mt76/patches/042-wifi-mt76-fix-queue-assignment-for-disassoc-packets.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@
+From 3999d15cfcc72a946ec419c4059b0e0cd7860053 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Peter Chiu <chui-hao.chiu@mediatek.com>
+Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 15:04:30 +0000
+Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: fix queue assignment for disassoc packets
+
+Like deauth, a disassoc frame sent to a client in powersave mode can get
+stuck in a tx queue along with other buffered frames, filling up hardware
+queues with frames that are only released after the WTBL slot is reused
+for another client.
+
+Move disassoc packets to the ALTX queue, matching the existing deauth
+handling.
+
+Fixes: dedf2ec30fe4 ("wifi: mt76: fix queue assignment for deauth packets")
+Signed-off-by: Peter Chiu <chui-hao.chiu@mediatek.com>
+Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20260727150434.1778520-11-nbd@nbd.name
+Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
+
+[W1700K staging note, 2026-09-01: from nbd168/wireless 3999d15cfcc7 (Felix's
+upstream staging tree, 2026-07-27). NOT in openwrt/mt76 (tx.c history checked)
+nor in our pin 2c84469c. Prerequisite for 043 (its tx.c context includes this
+line). Paths rewritten from drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/ to package
+root. Drop when a mt76 bump brings it.]
+
+Rebased 2026-09-03 on top of upstream 0898393ee0 ("wifi: mt76: use ALTX queue for
+packets to disassociated stations", = our former 043) for the mt76 be5ce791 bump.
+---
+--- a/tx.c
++++ b/tx.c
+@@ -695,6 +695,7 @@
+ 		    (!(wcid->tx_info & MT_WCID_TX_INFO_SET) ||
+ 		     !ieee80211_is_bufferable_mmpdu(skb) ||
+ 		     ieee80211_is_deauth(hdr->frame_control) ||
++		     ieee80211_is_disassoc(hdr->frame_control) ||
+ 		     head == &wcid->tx_offchannel))
+ 			qid = MT_TXQ_PSD;
+
diff --git a/package/kernel/mt76/patches/026-wifi-mt76-mt7996-validate-sta_num-in-all_sta_info-event.patch b/package/kernel/mt76/patches/026-wifi-mt76-mt7996-validate-sta_num-in-all_sta_info-event.patch
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/package/kernel/mt76/patches/026-wifi-mt76-mt7996-validate-sta_num-in-all_sta_info-event.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,57 @@
+From: mt76 upstream <linux-wireless>
+Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: validate sta_num in ALL_STA_INFO event
+
+Validate the firmware-reported station count against the actual received
+event size before iterating, to prevent an out-of-bounds read on a
+malformed or oversized UNI ALL_STA_INFO event. Also null-check skb_pull()
+and verify the event header itself fits in the skb.
+
+W1700K note: pure hardening, no behaviour change on well-formed events.
+Applies to our mt76 pin (b2704cf5); relevant to the per-station
+rate/ADM/MSDU-count path we consume (FlowSense WiFi stats + the tx_free
+MSDU_CNT handling in patch 019). Paths are mt76-source-relative (mt7996/).
+---
+--- a/mt7996/mcu.c
++++ b/mt7996/mcu.c
+@@ -648,13 +648,37 @@ static void
+ mt7996_mcu_rx_all_sta_info_event(struct mt7996_dev *dev, struct sk_buff *skb)
+ {
+ 	struct mt7996_mcu_all_sta_info_event *res;
+-	u16 i;
++	size_t elem_size;
++	u16 i, sta_num;
+
+-	skb_pull(skb, sizeof(struct mt7996_mcu_rxd));
++	if (!skb_pull(skb, sizeof(struct mt7996_mcu_rxd)))
++		return;
++
++	if (skb->len < sizeof(*res))
++		return;
+
+ 	res = (struct mt7996_mcu_all_sta_info_event *)skb->data;
+
+-	for (i = 0; i < le16_to_cpu(res->sta_num); i++) {
++	switch (le16_to_cpu(res->tag)) {
++	case UNI_ALL_STA_TXRX_RATE:
++		elem_size = sizeof(res->rate[0]);
++		break;
++	case UNI_ALL_STA_TXRX_ADM_STAT:
++		elem_size = sizeof(res->adm_stat[0]);
++		break;
++	case UNI_ALL_STA_TXRX_MSDU_COUNT:
++		elem_size = sizeof(res->msdu_cnt[0]);
++		break;
++	default:
++		return;
++	}
++
++	/* the firmware-provided station count must fit in the received event */
++	sta_num = le16_to_cpu(res->sta_num);
++	if (sta_num > (skb->len - sizeof(*res)) / elem_size)
++		return;
++
++	for (i = 0; i < sta_num; i++) {
+ 		u8 ac;
+ 		u16 wlan_idx;
+ 		struct mt76_wcid *wcid;
+
diff --git a/package/kernel/mt76/patches/044-wifi-mt76-mt7996-validate-tlv-length-in-ie-countdown.patch b/package/kernel/mt76/patches/044-wifi-mt76-mt7996-validate-tlv-length-in-ie-countdown.patch
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/package/kernel/mt76/patches/044-wifi-mt76-mt7996-validate-tlv-length-in-ie-countdown.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,51 @@
+From: New_patches (origin unknown, evaluated 2026-09-08)
+Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: validate TLV length in mt7996_mcu_ie_countdown
+
+The IE countdown event parser walked the TLV list using only a non-zero
+length as its loop guard.  A TLV whose length runs past the end of the
+skb was still dereferenced (event->omac_idx read from beyond tail), and
+a length smaller than the TLV header would not advance the cursor.
+
+Bound each tag to the skb, require it to be at least the header size so
+the loop always makes progress, and only read the countdown payload when
+the tag actually carries one.  Mirrors the tag_len checks mainline already
+applies in the all_sta_info event parser (see 026).
+
+Status: not in openwrt/mt76 be5ce791 (HEAD 2026-09-08) nor torvalds master.
+Applies to pin with all in-tree patches at offset +237, fuzz 0.
+
+diff --git a/mt7996/mcu.c b/mt7996/mcu.c
+index cd7587ce5b8a6..f74c4b0bda3c1 100644
+--- a/mt7996/mcu.c
++++ b/mt7996/mcu.c
+@@ -497,10 +497,18 @@ mt7996_mcu_ie_countdown(struct mt7996_dev *dev, struct sk_buff *skb)
+ 
+ 	tail = skb->data + skb->len;
+ 	data += sizeof(*hdr);
+-	while (data + sizeof(*tlv) < tail && le16_to_cpu(tlv->len)) {
++	while (data + sizeof(*tlv) <= tail) {
++		u16 tag_len = le16_to_cpu(tlv->len);
++
++		if (tag_len < sizeof(*tlv) || data + tag_len > tail)
++			break;
++
+ 		event = (struct mt7996_mcu_countdown_notify *)tlv->data;
+ 
+-		cdata.omac_idx = event->omac_idx;
++		if (tag_len >= sizeof(*tlv) + sizeof(*event))
++			cdata.omac_idx = event->omac_idx;
++		else
++			break;
+ 
+ 		switch (le16_to_cpu(tlv->tag)) {
+ 		case UNI_EVENT_IE_COUNTDOWN_CSA:
+@@ -517,7 +525,7 @@ mt7996_mcu_ie_countdown(struct mt7996_dev *dev, struct sk_buff *skb)
+ 			break;
+ 		}
+ 
+-		data += le16_to_cpu(tlv->len);
++		data += tag_len;
+ 		tlv = (struct tlv *)data;
+ 	}
+ }
+
